{"ref":"BDB, אֵת⁴","hw":"אֵת⁴","html":"† III. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אֵת</span>]</big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] a cutting instrument of iron, usually transl. <strong>ploughshare</strong>—sg. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵתוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 13:20\" href=\"/I_Samuel.13.20\">1 S 13:20</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵתִים</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 13:21\" href=\"/I_Samuel.13.21\">1 S 13:21</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 2:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.2.4\">Is 2:4</a> = <a data-ref=\"Micah 4:3\" href=\"/Micah.4.3\">Mi 4:3</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִתֵּיכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:10\" href=\"/Joel.4.10\">Jo 4:10</a>; according to Klo al. also <a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:5\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.5\">2 K 6:5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶת־הַבַּרְזֶל</span>, i.e. <em>the axe of iron</em>.","next":"BDB, ב","prev":"BDB, אתת"}